From 705afed8479babb27026e985830ecde215235345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:17:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 867/913] clk: stm32: fix priv resource leak in hse monitoring
 probe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

stm32_hse_monitoring() allocates priv with calloc() then returns early
on several paths (node not found, monitor node disabled, or clock
lookup failure) before priv is handed to register_pm_driver_cb(),
leaking the allocation. Move calloc to fix the issue.

Coverity issue: CID 1200442: Resource leak

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 99b8e34ee8b738350aa67ef40358946680e4b822 clk: stm32: fix priv resource leak in hse monitoring probe]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Sonnet-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I75cbaf43971df3b96ea4c07768e54c0406e3f91e
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/592843
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/clk/stm32/clk-stm32mp-hse-monitoring.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/clk/stm32/clk-stm32mp-hse-monitoring.c b/core/drivers/clk/stm32/clk-stm32mp-hse-monitoring.c
index 54386a498..09d7cd9e9 100644
--- a/core/drivers/clk/stm32/clk-stm32mp-hse-monitoring.c
+++ b/core/drivers/clk/stm32/clk-stm32mp-hse-monitoring.c
@@ -78,10 +78,6 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_hse_monitoring(void)
 	int node = -1;
 	TEE_Result res = TEE_ERROR_GENERIC;
 
-	priv = calloc(1, sizeof(*priv));
-	if (!priv)
-		return TEE_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY;
-
 	fdt = get_embedded_dt();
 	if (!fdt)
 		panic();
@@ -120,6 +116,10 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_hse_monitoring(void)
 	counter = fdt_counter_get(fdt, node, &config);
 	assert(counter && config);
 
+	priv = calloc(1, sizeof(*priv));
+	if (!priv)
+		return TEE_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY;
+
 	priv->counter = counter;
 	priv->config = config;
 	priv->threshold = ticks;
-- 
